          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "kersey, a kind of coarse narrow cloth, woven from long-staple wool and usually ribbed, originally produced in Kersey in Suffolk; reckoned at three to a shortcloth of assize (equivalent to one third of a pannus curtus) (OED s.v. kersey). See also pannus strictus."
    }
